From d96f16bbb510c01ae3c0ed3292e775cff94fe93e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 17:13:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Ship denoiser V8: albedo demodulation, sigma schedule,
 dither, gradient depth stop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The full improvement set, each change tested in isolation against a CPU-mirrored
harness before landing (Scratchpad/DenoiserLab in the session workspace):

- Albedo demodulation (+7.7 dB overall, +11.4 dB on textured surfaces): the
  kernel divides the mean by the primary albedo before the DenoiseImage store,
  so the a-trous filter smooths IRRADIANCE; the final level multiplies the
  albedo back at the presentation write. The albedo travels in OutputImage —
  unwritten while the denoiser owns the presentation — so the change needs no
  new image and no new binding (0-31 are taken and 31 must stay last). The
  divide uses the rgba8-quantised albedo so demodulate/remodulate are exact
  inverses; the variance channel rescales by the albedo luminance squared.
- Young-history variance floor (+0.61 dB in n=2 disocclusions, other pixels
  bit-identical): two or three agreeing samples can no longer certify ~0
  variance and freeze the filter on a fresh pixel.
- Per-level sigma_l schedule {4,4,2,1,1} (+0.42 dB, fresh glints 86.9->92.4%):
  the luminance stop tightens as the taps widen.
- Log-space luminance stop (glint retention 100%/97.7%): the edge-stop compares
  log(1+L), one sigma means the same step in shadow and highlight.
- Variance-gated firefly clamp: converged bright features are signal; only
  statistically uncertain brightness is clamped.
- Min-magnitude depth-gradient stop (+0.67 dB across a 0.4-unit step): the
  depth tolerance follows the surface's own gradient, so a slope filters along
  itself while a genuine step stops the kernel; one-sided differences combined
  by min magnitude so an edge cannot inflate its own tolerance.
- Half-LSB positional dither at the 8-bit write (sky banding 185->249 levels).

The kernel-to-denoise barrier now also covers the presentation image (the
final level reads the parked albedo). M9 gate updated with the change: the
mirror parks unit albedo, presentation assertions allow the half-LSB dither
bound, moved pins follow their lines (B10/B15/B27) — 97/97 GREEN, including
A5 which was stale on this branch since #27B added the sky-reservoir bit.
